    <text>
        <body>
            <div xml:id="d621">

                <pb facs="0682" n="674" xml:id="pg674"/>

                <note rend="inline" type="source">124.60C/89: Telegram</note>
                <head><hi rendition="#italic">The Ambassador in Poland</hi> (<hi rendition="#italic"
                        >Biddle</hi>) <hi rendition="#italic">to the Secretary of State</hi></head>
                <opener>
                    <dateline rendition="#float-right"><placeName><hi rendition="#small-caps"
                                >Warsaw</hi></placeName>, <date calendar="gregorian"
                            when="1939-09-05T10:00:00+01:00">September 5, 1939—10
                        a.m.</date><lb/>[Received September 5—7:42 a.m.]</dateline>
                </opener>
                <p>260. 1. In view of (<hi rendition="#italic">a</hi>) increased violence of aerial
                    attacks over Warsaw and (<hi rendition="#italic">b</hi>) turn for worse on
                    northern front whereby German troops have made considerable advance towards
                    Warsaw during past 24 hours,<anchor n="8" xml:id="d621-f1"/> the Polish
                    Government decided early this morning to initiate gradual evacuation of
                    Government offices and foreign diplomatic missions from Warsaw, latter to
                    Naleczow situated 23 kilometers west of Lublin. This adjacent to locality
                    whereto Foreign Minister and staff propose shortly to move.</p>
                <p>2. Accordingly, this evening will start evacuating by stages taking confidential
                    codes.</p>
                <p>3. Will advise you later of address as to where we can reestablish
                    communications.</p>
                <p>4. Military Attaché and Harrison<anchor n="9" xml:id="d621-f2"/> remaining in
                    Warsaw at Chancery until final evacuation is ordered of which you will be
                    notified.</p>
                <closer><signed><hi rendition="#small-caps">Biddle</hi></signed></closer>
            </div>
        </body>
    </text>
    <standOff>
        <listAnnotation>
            <note corresp="#d621-f1" n="8" xml:id="d621-f1-content">
                <p>For correspondence concerning the invasion of Poland by Germany, see <ref
                        target="frus1939v01#pg_402">vol. <hi rendition="#small-caps">i</hi>, pp.
                        402</ref> ff.</p>
            </note>
            <note corresp="#d621-f2" n="9" xml:id="d621-f2-content">
                <p>Landreth M. Harrison, Second Secretary of Embassy in Poland.</p>
            </note>
        </listAnnotation>
    </standOff>
